Docker container on a cgroup v2 host (private cgroup namespace, so the
container's cgroup is the root): limited to 2 CPUs and 4 GiB. The NVIDIA
driver is loaded and knows two GPUs; the PCI bus also lists them, which must
be ignored. Two sockets: core id 0 exists on both, and processor 3 is a
hyper-thread of processor 2, so there are 3 physical cores.

Fixtures are kept in this txtar-like format ("-- path --" starts a file)
because real sysfs names contain ':', which Windows checkouts cannot hold.
